### GET all categories (seeded: Miscallaneous, Financial Passwords, Home, Work, Social Media, Shopping)
GET http://localhost:5142/category

###

### GET a specific category with its credentials (4 = Work: Google, Slack, GitHub)
GET http://localhost:5142/category/1

###

### CREATE a new category
POST http://localhost:5142/category
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "CategoryName": "Gaming"
}

###

### CREATE a duplicate category name -> expect 400 BadRequest
POST http://localhost:5142/category
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "CategoryName": "Work"
}

###

### UPDATE/rename a category (5 = Social Media)
PUT http://localhost:5142/category/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "CategoryName": "Socials"
}

###

### DELETE Miscallaneous (id 1) -> expect 400 BadRequest (cannot delete default)
DELETE http://localhost:5142/category/1

###

### DELETE Work (id 4) -> credentials migrate to Miscallaneous.
### Work has "Google"/"GitHub", which also exist elsewhere, so this exercises the name-collision handling.
DELETE http://localhost:5142/category/4
